INT. ORBITAL GREENHOUSE RING - SECTOR NINE - CONTINUOUS

Rows of dead tomato vines hang from the ceiling racks like gray rope. Emergency amber pulses. A hull alarm drones under everything.

CAPTAIN IRENKA VOSS, 50s, rail-thin, flight suit patched at the knees, slams a manual valve wheel. DUMISANI NKOSI, 30s, engineer, wedges a pry bar into a buckled bulkhead seam. PELL, 20s, the botanist, hugs a seed vault to his chest.

IRENKA
Everyone, pressure in ninety seconds. Move your feet.

DUMISANI
(to Pell)
Hold the light higher. Higher!

PELL
(muttering)
It's a tomato. It's just a tomato.

The bulkhead groans. Dumisani and Irenka heave on the bar together and the seam shrieks open six inches. A gust of cold air tears through, and all three duck, Pell clutching the vault, Dumisani losing his grip, Irenka grabbing his collar.

IRENKA
Nobody lets go of anything!

PELL
(to himself)
Breathe, breathe, breathe.

DUMISANI
Captain, the vault is not coming through that gap!

IRENKA
Then the vault goes first and we follow it.

She pushes Pell toward the opening. Pell and Dumisani both freeze as the alarm changes pitch, a rising whine. Irenka looks up at the ceiling vents. She shoves them both through and dives in after.
